# async stdlib basic smoke test
# Tests the pure-LLT functions in stdlib/async.llt that do not require
# the async runtime (task/await/channel) to be live — specifically:
#   - retry: succeeds on first attempt
#   - finally: runs cleanup and returns body value on success
#   - finally: runs cleanup and re-raises on error
#   - await-all: wraps map-await (tested via identity since no async runtime)
#
# Note: loop-select, recv-all, await-all, and shutdown stubs (exit,
# graceful-exit) are not tested here because they require either a live
# async runtime or builtins not yet implemented.

[include %libdir "async.llt"]
[retry 3 [fn [] 42]]
=== out
Int(42)
